Hi all,

We have a tricky case of a game crash on which we need a decision (and probably
some help implenting that decision):

1)	eit_brad had a game crash on the Astral Plane, in a position where ascension
looks almost certain and with _lots_ of points; NetHack left no checkpoint
files or any other trace of the game.  Since he had the game recorder on, we
know his inventory and (since he had the showexp option on) we actually know
his experience points.  He wasn't aware the showscore option was available, so
that wasn't on.

The recording of the crash is publicly available at:

<http://nethack/cgi-bin/tournament/serve.pl?player=eit_brad&session=2003-11-06-0
9-22-10>

The final status line at the time the game crashed was:

Eit_brad the Roamer      St:18/** Dx:21 Co:18 In:18 Wi:18 Ch:18  Neutral
Astral Plane $:0  HP:230(230) Pw:33(33) AC:-41 Xp:20/6858364 T:69337

The decision here will probably be to give eit_brad credit for the game at a
point value equivalent to having #quit at the point where the game crashed,
since we should be able to manually calculate the score from his inventory and
experience points.

Are any of y'all sufficiently familiar with the NetHack score calculation to
save us some dredge work and calculate it for us?

Does this seem a reasonable and fair way of dealng with this?

